<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis XI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1423–1483</span> · Also known as Louis XI of France</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis XI was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1461 to 1483. He fought the great nobles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-the-public-weal">League of the Public Weal</a> and above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, whose death at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a> in 1477 allowed him to seize the Duchy of Burgundy, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a>. He also crushed the counts of Armagnac and acquired Anjou and Provence, greatly enlarging the royal domain. His cunning earned him the name 'the universal spider'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-xi.jpg" alt="Louis XI" width="320" height="525" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob de Litemont · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_XI_(1423-1483).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
